


The parse function "parse.h"

            If #1 does not point to a string, the behavior
            is undefined.
              The parse function finds the first character
            in the string that is not a word-separator and
            stores the corresponding index in the first
            element of the array specified by #0.
              Then, the parse function finds the first
            character in the string that is a word-separator
            and stores the corresponding index in the second
            element of the array specified by #0.
